<title>SINGAPORE: Popular shares open at 33 pct premium.</title>
<headline>Popular shares open at 33 pct premium.</headline>
<dateline>SINGAPORE 1997-05-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>Share dealing in publishing firm Popular Holdings Ltd began on the Stock Exchange of Singapore on Friday, with the stock opening at a 33 percent premium of Singapore $0.48 over its S$0.36 offer price.</p>
<p>The shares continued their climb in the first 10 minutes of trade, hitting a high of S$0.535 with 16 million shares changing hands.</p>
<p>Popular said on Thursday its initial public offer (IPO) of 56.25 million shares had been 28 times subscribed.</p>
<p>Small investors got 36.2 percent of the shares.</p>
<p>-- Singapore newsroom (65 8703011)</p>
</text>
